 ### Are epistasis and empirical omega p-value options production-stable?
 
-Not yet. In current CLI help, epistasis-related options and `--calc_omega_pvalue` options are marked as **Experimental feature** and default to off unless explicitly enabled.
+Not yet. Both remain experimental and default to off. The `epistasis_*`
+options implement exploratory structure weighting, not an epistasis test.
+Active fixed/auto beta requires independent branch context and
+`--expectation_method urn --asrv sn`. Tuning and predictions exclude held-out
+monophyletic clades; self-response context is no longer supported. Positive beta
+is not evidence of epistasis. Omega P values cannot currently be combined with
+this weighting. See the [input contract and validation limits](https://github.com/kfuku52/csubst/blob/master/docs/STRUCTURE_WEIGHTING.md).
 
 ### How to find v0.20.17 used in Fukushima & Pollock (2023)?
 The latest release is recommended for general use. If you need the legacy version v0.20.17 referenced in [Fukushima & Pollock (2023)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41559-022-01932-7), it is available at the link below.
